Z||000000||BroCar 87||11-29-2000||04:15 AM||||Hey guys, I was wondering if I can swap my horn paddled steering wheel for the three spoked FORMULA steering wheel. They are both offered in fieros, so I would think I can. Can anyone tell me how I would go about doing this?<BR>Thanks for any help.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||11-29-2000||08:14 AM||||Pretty sure all are interchangable but Formulas have the paddle wheel as standard, the 3 spoke is on GTs||||reg||1
Z||000002||BBBAD GT||11-29-2000||08:16 AM||||Yes, they are interchangable.  Just get a balancer puller (rent one from autozone) and you'll have no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BroCar 87||11-29-2000||02:01 PM||||Thanks guys. Im off to swap steering wheels!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Bro outt!!!||||reg||6
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||11-29-2000||03:24 PM||||I just did the same thing last week. Just make sure you have a steering wheel puller. I works fine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||11-29-2000||04:04 PM||||Just be sure to get the horn connection when you get the wheel.  We swapped the 4 spoke paddle steering wheel in my daughter's 87 coupe for a 3 spoke vinyl covered wheel out of an 84 SE.  The wheel fit fine but I also needed the horn connector to get the wiring to work right.  Cost me another trip to the salvage yard to get the connector off the 84.<P>Personnally I much prefer the 3 spoke design from the GT or earlier SE models.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
